From a29f0fdd67dbed65140faa4b271f117ba9b97009 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 17:00:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Three things from a play session: ice that would not cast, a
 pouch that lied, two shops the wrong way round

ONE EFFECTIVE ICE SPELL LOCKED YOU OUT OF ICE SPELLS. ~pvm_freeze_allowed refused the
WHOLE cast at a target that was already frozen - no damage, no runes spent, just "Your
target is already held by a magical force" for the length of the freeze the previous
cast had applied. Keeping a barrage on a frozen target is the entire point of the spell.

The same file already knew the right answer and was applying it to the wrong half. Its
secondary-target path carries the comment "an already-frozen secondary target is left
alone rather than having its freeze refreshed" and guards only the FREEZE, letting the
damage land. The primary target's path refused the spell outright.

AND THE TABLE ALREADY SAID WHICH SPELLS MAY BE REFUSED, so nothing here had to be
decided: Bind, Snare and Entangle carry `data=maxhit,-1` because the freeze IS the
spell, and every ancient ice spell carries a real one. ~magic_spell_is_pure_freeze reads
that, and only a pure freeze is now turned away at a held target - which keeps the
message the OSRS wiki's Snare page quotes, for the three spells it belongs to.

~pvm_freeze_lands / ~pvp_freeze_lands is now the one rule for whether a freeze takes,
used by the primary and the secondary path alike, and it honours the five-tick immunity
that follows a freeze - which the secondary path's own version did not.

THE RUNE POUCH MIRROR OUTLIVED THE POUCH. rune_pouch_mirror:runes was transmitted once
from login and never touched again, so the client kept counting the pouch's runes after
the pouch had been banked, dropped or died with: every spell lit up and every cast was
then refused by the server, which checks properly. "It says I have the runes and I can't
cast anything" is exactly that.

There is no [inv_changed] trigger in this engine, so a softtimer asks every other tick
and re-transmits only when the answer CHANGES - the store when the pouch is carried, an
inv that is empty by config when it is not. NOT inv_stoptransmit, which would leave the
client holding its last copy, which is the bug.

THE EQUIPMENT STORE IS EAST OF THE ORE AND GEM STORE, and ours were the other way round.
That is the one thing about their placement the OSRS wiki actually states, and the two
Hur spawns in m38_80 are swapped to honour it. Their absolute tiles are still this
fork's own - picked by flooding the city from Mej-Jal - and claude/tzhaar-shops-and-
tzrek-jad.md has always said so. Three ::tele coords would fix that properly.

playfixes_battery.py is 4 groups, ALL PASS; playfixes_mutate.py breaks 17 things and
every one is caught by its own check. Both are in CI.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015mjzJ5S7cQ1h1aE5KeBabD
